    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "net: stop monitoring select exceptions outside Windows",
    "user": {
      "login": "Sjors",
      "id": 10217,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjE3",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10217?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Sjors",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Sjors/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Alternative approach to #36688, citing the relevant parts of its description:\r\n\r\n> There is currently nothing preventing us to receive TCP urgent data, which would never be returned by `recv()`. Linux's `poll()` is indifferent to this, but the `select()` socket monitoring may keep reporting it as pending on some platforms.\r\n> \r\n> This would not prevent progress nor lead to a crash anymore after #36665, but it's still undesirable.\r\n\r\nFix this by ignoring the exceptionSet. Except on Windows, where we instead disconnect if its used.\r\n\r\nWe could instead have set `SO_OOBINLINE` on our sockets, so `recv()` returns any urgent data sent to us (and likely leads us to disconnect the peer). But this goes against the spirit of RFC 6093, as documented in the second commit.\r\n\r\n",
