      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/1fde57f1deda683129ccead9c30cfad0e235914e",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "2b9834965411a7f6d9cf10ae30da92ffffeb3098",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/2b9834965411a7f6d9cf10ae30da92ffffeb3098"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 2b9834965411a7f6d9cf10ae30da92ffffeb3098\nparent ab7e668cc6af5d716ad40166d1f88235a2f6d25d\nauthor Sjors Provoost <sjors@sprovoost.nl> 1793419213 +0000\ncommitter Sjors Provoost <sjors@sprovoost.nl> 1793419213 +0000\n\nnet: stop monitoring select exceptions outside Windows\n\nWindows needs select's exception set to detect failed non-blocking\nconnects. On other platforms, a TCP urgent pointer can leave the\nexception set pending even when no data is readable. Only monitor it\non Windows, and disconnect established P2P peers if it is set.\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Poinsot <mail@antoinep.com>\n",
